Asim Munir’s military-backed regime and its handlers are using live ammunition against peaceful demonstrations to protect their power. For four years since the regime change, anyone taking to the streets in peaceful protest has been met with direct gunfire.

Never in Pakistan’s history have live bullets been fired directly at peaceful demonstrators within their own country. The violent crackdown is a war for personal power that comes at the direct expense of the nation.

